---
/*
 * Section 4 — how we decide what to build.
 *
 * NO NUMBERED STEPS AND NO PROCESS DIAGRAM, ANYWHERE ON THIS PAGE. The copy file makes
 * it a build note and gives two reasons, both right: a staged treatment makes the
 * engagement feel long, and it duplicates what the industry pages already do —
 * /accounting and /workshop both carry a stepper, and this page is not a third pitch.
 * So this is three paragraphs of prose and a pull quote, and the temptation to number
 * "assessment first, business case second, build only if the case holds" into a 1-2-3
 * should be resisted. It is a sentence. It reads as one.
 *
 * THE PULL QUOTE CARRIES THE BAND. With no illustration and no stepper, the section is
 * otherwise a heading and three paragraphs, which on a 1240px container is a column of
 * prose with a third of the band empty beside it. The quote runs the full width, set
 * large on a terracotta rule, and it is also the most quotable line on the site — "we
 * would rather tell you not to build something than sell you something that isn't worth
 * the money" is a position, not a claim, and it is what the whole page is evidence for.
 *
 * THE THIRD PARAGRAPH CARRIES THE LINK TO /workshop that the copy file's SEO section
 * asks for, on the words "a workshop that ranks them first". That is the natural anchor:
 * it is the sentence describing the thing, so the link goes where a reader would look
 * for it rather than being bolted on at the end.
 *
 * "SOME AREN'T WORTH FIXING AT THIS SIZE OF BUSINESS, AND SAYING SO IS PART OF THE WORK
 * RATHER THAN A FAILURE OF IT" is the sentence the pull quote is built on, and it must
 * not be softened into a hedge. Blame the work, never the owner: it says the fix isn't
 * worth it at this size, not that the business is too small to deserve one.
 */
---

<section class="section section--white decide" id="how-we-decide">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head decide__head">
      <h2 class="section__title decide__title">
        Assessment first. Business case second. Build only if the case holds.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="decide__grid">
      <div class="decide__body">
      <p class="decide__para">
        We start by examining how the work actually moves &mdash; with the people who
        perform it, not only the people who describe it. We establish where time and money
        go, put figures against each candidate using your numbers, and state every
        assumption openly so you can challenge it.
      </p>

      <p class="decide__para">
        Then we test each candidate against what AI genuinely does today. Some are AI
        problems. Some need a change to the order the work happens in. Some need better
        use of software you already license. Some aren&rsquo;t worth fixing at this size
        of business, and saying so is part of the work rather than a failure of it.
      </p>

      <p class="decide__para">
        If the case holds, we build it, on accounts you own, and hand it back operating.
        If you can&rsquo;t yet name the one process to examine, we run
        <a href="/workshop">a workshop that ranks them first</a> &mdash; a day on one
        agreed area of your operation.
      </p>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="decide__quote">
        <p>
          We would rather tell you not to build something than sell you something that
          isn&rsquo;t worth the money.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .decide__head {
    max-width: none;
  }

  .decide__title {
    max-width: 26ch;
  }

  /* SPLIT BY CONTENT TYPE — all the prose in one column, the quote in the other. That is
   * the site's standing rule for a two-column section and it is the second thing tried
   * here. The first was `columns: 2` across the three paragraphs, which does not divide:
   * three paragraphs into two columns is 1 + 2, so the left column ended a full paragraph
   * short and the quote sat under a visible hole. Flowing text across columns also makes
   * the reader travel to the bottom of the band and back up again, for no gain.
   *
   * The quote earns the right-hand column because with no illustration anywhere on this
   * page it is the only thing that can fill one. */
  .decide__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.85fr);
    column-gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .decide__para {
    font-size: var(--ark-body);
    line-height: var(--ark-lh-body);
    color: var(--ark-body-ink);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .decide__para + .decide__para {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .decide__para a {
    color: var(--ark-terracotta-ink);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  /* The band-filler. See the note at the top of this file. */
  .decide__quote {
    padding: 22px 0 22px 32px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--ark-terracotta);
  }

  .decide__quote p {
    font-family: var(--ark-font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.22;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--ark-ink);
    max-width: 26ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    /* One column, in DOM order: the prose, then the quote it earns. */
    .decide__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      row-gap: 28px;
      margin-top: 26px;
    }

    .decide__para {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .decide__para + .decide__para {
      margin-top: 14px;
    }

    .decide__quote {
      padding: 16px 0 16px 18px;
    }

    .decide__quote p {
      font-size: 1.375rem;
      max-width: 22ch;
    }
  }
</style>
